Chapter: BvtCityDoors
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtNpcMove
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UOAIX-260 (trial 44375): city 0's map is Britain's walk map, whose colliders hold the decoration's doors, so a Britain
 city worker steps with Britain's doors; every other city's map holds no doors and steps with none.
  bvt-city-doors : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-city-doors (unused) = when bnm-founded 0
    is Err (e) -> bvt-check ("city doors fixture: " & e) False
    is Ok (owner) -> act
      a <- bvt-check "a Britain city worker (city 0) steps with Britain's bound doors (cg-city-doors)" (when owner.town-doors is None -> False is Just (_) -> (when cg-city-doors owner 0 is None -> False is Just (_) -> True))
      b <- bvt-check "a worker of any other city steps with no doors (cg-city-doors 5, 8)" ((when cg-city-doors owner 5 is None -> True is Just (_) -> False) & (when cg-city-doors owner 8 is None -> True is Just (_) -> False))
      a + b
    end
